# macho module

The `macho` module parses Mach-O files for macOS and Apple Silicon targets.

## Constants

Magic values:

- `MH_MAGIC`, `MH_CIGAM`
- `MH_MAGIC_64`, `MH_CIGAM_64`
- `FAT_MAGIC`, `FAT_CIGAM`
- `FAT_MAGIC_64`, `FAT_CIGAM_64`

## Types

### `CpuType`

Mach-O CPU type.

- `name(self)`: return a readable name.

### `FileType`

Mach-O file type.

- `name(self)`: return a readable name.

### `CommandType`

Load command type.

- `name(self)`: return a readable name.

### `SectionType`

Mach-O section type.

- `name(self)`: return a readable name.

### `Section64`

64-bit section descriptor.

Methods:

- `getSectName(self)`: section name.
- `getSegName(self)`: segment name.
- `getAlignment(self)`: alignment.
- `getType(self)`: section type.
- `isZeroFill(self)`: true for zero-fill sections.
- `hasInstructions(self)`: true for code sections.
- `getData(self, file_bytes)`: section bytes.
- `parseRelocation(self, file_bytes, endian, index)`: parse one relocation.
- `parseAllRelocations(self, allocator, file_bytes, endian)`: parse all relocations.

### `Nlist64`

64-bit nlist symbol entry.

Methods:

- `isStab`, `isExternal`, `isPrivateExternal`.
- `getType`, `isUndefined`, `isCommon`, `isAbsolute`, `isSection`, `isIndirect`.
- `isWeakDef`, `isWeakRef`.
- `getLibraryOrdinal`.
- `getName(self, strtab_bytes)`: symbol name.
- `typeName(self)`: readable type name.

### `Segment64Command`

64-bit segment load command.

Methods:

- `getName(self)`: segment name.
- `isExecutable`, `isWritable`, `isReadable`.
- `parseSection(self, endian, index)`: parse one section.
- `parseAllSections(self, allocator, endian)`: parse all sections.

### `SymtabCommand`

Symbol table load command.

Methods:

- `getStringTable(self, file_bytes)`: string table bytes.
- `parseSymbol(self, file_bytes, endian, index)`: parse one symbol.
- `parseAllSymbols(self, allocator, file_bytes, endian)`: parse all symbols.

### `DysymtabCommand`, `MainCommand`, `DylibCommand`, `BuildVersionCommand`

Load command payloads. `DylibCommand.getName` and `BuildVersionCommand.platformName` read their data.

### `LoadCommand`

Generic load command.

Methods convert it to a specific command type:

- `asSegment64`, `asSymtab`, `asDysymtab`, `asMain`, `asDylib`, `asBuildVersion`.

### `LoadCommandIterator`

- `next(self)`: return the next load command or null.

### `Header`

Parsed Mach-O header.

Methods:

- `isObject`, `isExecutable`, `isDylib`, `isPie`.
- `headerSize(self)`: header size in bytes.
- `parse(bytes)`: parse the header.
- `loadCommands(self, file_bytes)`: return a load command iterator.

### `Relocation`

Mach-O relocation entry.

- `byteSize(self)`: size in bytes.
- `typeName(self, cpu)`: readable type name.

## Functions

- `parseRelocation(bytes, endian)`: parse one relocation.
- `parseNlist64(bytes, endian)`: parse one nlist entry.
- `parseSection64(bytes, endian)`: parse one section.

## Constant groups

- `flags`: Mach-O header flags.
- `section_attributes`: section attribute flags.
- `vm_prot`: virtual memory protection flags.
- `nlist_masks`, `nlist_type`, `nlist_desc`: symbol entry masks and flags.
- `reloc_constants`: relocation constants such as `R_SCATTERED`.

## Constant groups

`sibl.macho_flags` contains Mach-O header flags such as `NOUNDEFS`, `DYLDLINK`, `PIE`, `WEAK_DEFINES`, and others.

`sibl.macho_vm_prot` contains protection constants: `NONE`, `READ`, `WRITE`, and `EXECUTE`.

`sibl.macho_section_attributes` contains section attribute constants such as `PURE_INSTRUCTIONS`, `NO_DEAD_STRIP`, `DEBUG_INFO`, and `EXT_RELOC`.

`sibl.macho_nlist_masks`, `sibl.macho_nlist_type`, and `sibl.macho_nlist_desc` contain symbol entry masks and flags.

`sibl.macho_reloc_constants` contains relocation constants such as `R_SCATTERED`.

## Error sets

- `Error`
- `CommandError`
- `SectionError`
- `SymbolError`
- `RelocationError`

## Example

```zig
const macho_hdr = try sibl.macho.Header.parse(mapped.data);
var it = try macho_hdr.loadCommands(mapped.data);

while (try it.next()) |cmd| {
    if (cmd.cmd == .segment_64) {
        const seg = try cmd.asSegment64(macho_hdr.endian());
        std.debug.print("segment: {s}\n", .{seg.getName()});
    }
}
```

## Notes

- Use the header endian when parsing commands and symbols.
- Load commands follow the header.
- Sections live inside segment load commands.
- The parser keeps slices into the mapped file.
